==Portuguese==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|roa-opt|pt}} {{term|tomar|lang=roa-opt}}, of {{unk.|pt|title=unknown}} origin. Possibly derived from {{etyl|la|pt}} {{term|autumo|autumāre|I reckon; I affirm|lang=la}}<ref>Yakov Malkiel, ''Etymology''</ref>.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|Portugal}} {{IPA|/tuˈmaɾ/|lang=pt}}
* {{audio|Pt tomar.ogg|Audio}}
* {{homophones|Tomar|lang=pt}}

===Verb===
{{pt-verb|tom|ar}}

# {{context|transitive|lang=pt}} to [[take]] (something);
#: "''Fui ao banco '''tomar''' meu dinheiro.''" - I went to the bank to take my money.
# {{context|transitive|lang=pt}} to [[steal]] (something);
#: "''O ladrão '''tomou''' todo o meu dinheiro.''" - The thief has stolen all my money.
# {{context|transitive|lang=pt}} to consider that something or someone (direct object) is other thing or other one (''[[por]]'');
#: "''Eu '''tomei''' a Maria por corrupta.''" - I thought Mary was corrupt.
# {{context|transitive|lang=pt}} to [[drink]];
#: "''Eu '''tomei''' suco.''" - I drank juice.
# {{context|intransitive|lang=pt}} to [[consume]] [[alcoholic]] [[beverage]]s;
#: "''Ele '''toma''' muito, durante os finais de semana.''" - He drinks a lot, on weekends.

====Conjugation====
{{pt-conj|tom|ar}}

